  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pc23:1.2": "“Nunnery” renders <i lang='pi' translate='no'>upassaya</i>. According to the word definition below, this includes any place where a nun stays. In other words, it spans anything from a single hut, see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-bi-vb-pc35/en/brahmali#1.23.1'>Bi Pc 35</a>, to a monastery. The Jain text The Ācārāṅga-sūtra, contains a passage that describes an <i lang='pi' translate='no'>upassaya</i> as including a grassy area, that is, it must have been a compound of buildings or a monastery: “A layman might, for the sake of a mendicant … cutting and clipping the grass outside or within the upāśraya (= <i lang='pi' translate='no'>upassaya</i>).” See Jacobi, Hermann, trans. “Jaina Sutras Part I”. Motilal Babarsidass, 1964, p. 94. ",
